  "name": "jerboa",
  "_about": "a LESSER EGYPTIAN JERBOA (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/small/jerboa.py, written in its standing pose, sk.py): a desert hopping mouse, not a kangaroo -- 10 cm held half upright on two very long hind legs (the foot alone 5 cm, three long middle toes, hair-cushioned beneath), the tiny forelegs held up under the chin; a mouse's round head with a short pointed muzzle and long whiskers, huge dark eyes, big thin rounded ears; an 18 cm string-thin tail ending in a flat tuft, black then white; sandy buff over pure white, a pale hip stripe. It hops, both feet together. Coats: lesser Egyptian, long-eared (greyer; the variant `long-eared` has the enormous ears), great jerboa (1.5x)",
